m/india/get-ready-to-lose-2029-polls-amit-shah-warns-rahul-gandhi-with-congress-poll-history/articleshow/134920449.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-13T20:14:52+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Karan Manral</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134920698,imgsize-98339.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['We've found missing head of 11th century Khajuraho Vishnu idol, will be restored soon': ASI chief]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/weve-found-missing-head-of-11th-century-khajuraho-vishnu-idol-will-be-restored-soon-asi-chief/articleshow/134920422.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134920422.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Archaeological Survey of India has found the missing head of an 11th-century Vishnu idol at Khajuraho. ASI plans to restore the idol after examination and has introduced a three-year deadline for excavation projects. A preliminary excavation at Ujjain's Vaishya Tekri aims to determine the significance of newly identified structures. ASI is also addressing funding disparities based on visitor numbers and maintenance needs at various sites.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/weve-found-missing-head-of-11th-century-khajuraho-vishnu-idol-will-be-restored-soon-asi-chief/articleshow/134920422.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/weve-found-missing-head-of-11th-century-khajuraho-vishnu-idol-will-be-restored-soon-asi-chief/articleshow/134920422.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-13T20:08:13+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pankul Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134920586,imgsize-171382.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Lady hiding in Dehradun': Who was Rahul Gandhi referring to at INDIA bloc presser?]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/lady-hiding-in-dehradun-who-was-rahul-gandhi-referring-to-at-india-bloc-presser/articleshow/134919566.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134919566.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[During the INDIA bloc's press conference, Rahul Gandhi's reference to a "lady hiding right now in Dehradun" raised questions about whom he was referring to. The remark came amid the opposition's campaign against CEC Gyanesh Kumar over alleged electoral-roll irregularities.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/lady-hiding-in-dehradun-who-was-rahul-gandhi-referring-to-at-india-bloc-presser/articleshow/134919566.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/lady-hiding-in-dehradun-who-was-rahul-gandhi-referring-to-at-india-bloc-presser/articleshow/134919566.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-13T19:35:50+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Priyanka Mukherjee</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134919668,imgsize-1457760.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Agreed to build on positive momentum in ties': PM Modi speaks with Canada PM Mark Carney]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/agreed-to-build-on-positive-momentum-in-ties-pm-modi-speaks-with-canada-pm-mark-carney/articleshow/134919669.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134919669.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Prime Minister Narendra Modi and Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney discussed enhancing the strategic partnership between India and Canada. The leaders emphasized collaboration on trade, energy, technology, and security matters. Both nations aim to finalize a Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement by December to boost bilateral trade significantly. Modi's potential visit to Canada would mark his first since diplomatic tensions arose previously.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/agreed-to-build-on-positive-momentum-in-ties-pm-modi-speaks-with-canada-pm-mark-carney/articleshow/134919669.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/agreed-to-build-on-positive-momentum-in-ties-pm-modi-speaks-with-canada-pm-mark-carney/articleshow/134919669.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-13T19:17:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134919708,imgsize-65670.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Absence from draft SIR doesn't mean deletion': EC to Bombay HC]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/absence-from-draft-sir-doesnt-mean-deletion-ec-to-bombay-hc/articleshow/134919317.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134919317.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The Election Commission of India clarified that missing names from the draft electoral roll during the Special Intensive Revision do not imply their deletion. This declaration came amid a court hearing in response to a Goa resident's concern over their absent name. The petitioner expressed frustration that their address change application had not been processed on time.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/absence-from-draft-sir-doesnt-mean-deletion-ec-to-bombay-hc/articleshow/134919317.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/absence-from-draft-sir-doesnt-mean-deletion-ec-to-bombay-hc/articleshow/134919317.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-13T18:58:59+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134919394,imgsize-154620.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[High tea after street heat: What happened at INDIA bloc meet at Rahul Gandhi's residence]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/high-tea-after-street-heat-what-happened-at-india-bloc-meet-at-rahul-gandhis-residence/articleshow/134918043.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134918043.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Leaders from the INDIA bloc held a meeting at Rahul Gandhi's residence to protest vote theft allegations against Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar. They expressed their commitment to continue the protests and seek accountability from those responsible for undermining democracy. Various leaders spoke about the fight for fair elections and the need to hold officials accountable. They emphasized that their efforts would persist across the nation.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/high-tea-after-street-heat-what-happened-at-india-bloc-meet-at-rahul-gandhis-residence/articleshow/134918043.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/high-tea-after-street-heat-what-happened-at-india-bloc-meet-at-rahul-gandhis-residence/articleshow/134918043.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-13T18:58:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134919396,imgsize-165318.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Don’t want to spoil the surprise': Rahul Gandhi on INDIA bloc's next step in CEC-SIR row]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dont-want-to-spoil-the-surprise-rahul-gandhi-on-india-blocs-next-step-in-cec-sir-row/articleshow/134917355.cms"&g